# CODEOWNERS — who must review what.
#
# GitHub automatically requests a review from the owner when a PR touches a matching
# path. Combined with the "Require review from Code Owners" ruleset, these paths
# require approval from at least one listed owner.
#
# Syntax: <path pattern>  <@github-user>
# Last matching rule wins, so order matters — general first, specific last.
#
# An owner must have write access or better, or the rule SILENTLY DOES NOTHING.
# There is no warning. If reviews stop being requested, check repo access first.

# Everything, unless a more specific rule below overrides it.
*                                   @nair-akash @nanhangfei

# --- Critical paths ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# Listed separately from the catch-all so the intent survives when other owners
# are added. To hand an area to a teammate, add their @handle on that line — they
# only need write access to the repo. Nothing here requires GitHub Teams.
#
#   /services/api/app/narration/      @nair-akash @someone-else

